-- en/11-exec-help/argv --
crater job exec --help
-- en/11-exec-help/exit --
0
-- en/11-exec-help/stdout --
Open the task user's login shell when no command is given. Commands after -- retain argv boundaries and use that user's HOME and exported shell environment. --env-mode container skips environment probing. Select --pod and --container when there are multiple candidates; no SSH or GPU dependency.

Usage:
  crater job exec <name> [flags] [-- COMMAND [ARG...]]

Flags:
  -c, --container string   Select a running container by name
      --env-mode string    Environment source: user (default) or container (skip configuration probing) (default "user")
      --pod string         Select a pod belonging to the job
  -i, --stdin              Forward standard input to the command
  -t, --tty                Allocate a terminal (requires -i and local terminals)

Global Flags:
  -h, --help             Help for crater
      --json             Output in raw JSON format
      --no-interactive   Disable interactive prompts
-- en/11-exec-help/stderr --
-- en/12-ssh-help/argv --
crater job ssh --help
-- en/12-ssh-help/exit --
0
-- en/12-ssh-help/stdout --
Open SSH access and print host:port, or enter a session with --connect using local OpenSSH.

Usage:
  crater job ssh <name> [flags]

Flags:
      --connect                Connect immediately using local OpenSSH
  -i, --identity-file string   Private key file for --connect
      --user string            SSH username (default: task container user)

Global Flags:
  -h, --help             Help for crater
      --json             Output in raw JSON format
      --no-interactive   Disable interactive prompts
-- en/12-ssh-help/stderr --
